  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Did a fresh install on a new system, for evaluation purposes. Tomcat starts well when launched interactively (startup.bat). But registering Tomcat6.exe as a service (by service.bat), it refuses to start, and a system error event 7042 is logged, along with the fuzzy message: \"The Apache Tomcat 6 service terminated with service-specific error The operation completed successfully..\"",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "It turned out that the Tomcat binaries (tomcat6.exe, tomcat6w.exe) were 32-bit. Appearently, Win-2008-r2 doesn't like this in the windows service context. Replacing them by 64-bit binaries found elsewhere (apache-tomcat-6.0.29-windows-x64.zip), the service starts properly, but I didn't check it thoroughly, as i'm really a novice in this domain.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1
  },
  "duedate": null,
  "environment": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Win-2008-r2 which is 64-bit, VMware workstation",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
